// PRUSASLICER AS ITS OWN SUBJECT, SEPARATE FROM BAMBU STUDIO AND FROM THE MACHINE.
//
// DESIGN section 3 external decomposition: Bambu Studio is a FORK of PrusaSlicer and OrcaSlicer is a
// fork of Bambu Studio, so they are three independently versioned subjects that happen to share
// ancestry. extdeps.printing.bambu_studio already models one of them. This models another, and
// neither may enumerate the other.
//
// WHY THIS SUBJECT EXISTS AT ALL, recorded because it is a constraint and not a preference: every
// machine this repository owns is aarch64 -- the Ampere Altra hosts, the DGX Sparks, and the session
// containers. Bambu Studio and OrcaSlicer publish x86_64 Linux builds. PrusaSlicer is packaged for
// arm64 and was verified to slice headlessly on srv2 with no display server. It is the only slicer
// that runs on the hardware, which is why the profile has to be authored rather than downloaded.

// THE FLAVOUR VOCABULARY IS CLOSED, and the reason is measured rather than stylistic. Slicing the
// coupon with PrusaSlicer's default emitted `gcode_flavor = reprap`, while the Bambu-produced file
// the A1 mini actually printed carries `gcode_flavor = marlin`. A stringly flavour field would have
// let that difference be spelled two ways and compared as equal.
type PrusaSlicerGcodeFlavor
  = FlavorMarlin
  | FlavorMarlinFirmware
  | FlavorRepRap
  | FlavorKlipper

fn gcode_flavor_config_value(f: PrusaSlicerGcodeFlavor) -> NonEmptyStr {
  match f {
    FlavorMarlin => "marlin"
    FlavorMarlinFirmware => "marlin2"
    FlavorRepRap => "reprap"
    FlavorKlipper => "klipper"
  }
}

data prusa_slicer_gcode_flavors: List<PrusaSlicerGcodeFlavor> = [
  FlavorMarlin,
  FlavorMarlinFirmware,
  FlavorRepRap,
  FlavorKlipper,
]
